Main article: [ Chlorinated polyvinyl chloride
](/wiki/Chlorinated_polyvinyl_chloride "Chlorinated polyvinyl chloride")

PVC can be usefully modified by chlorination, which increases its chlorine
content to or above 67%. [ Chlorinated polyvinyl chloride
](/wiki/Chlorinated_polyvinyl_chloride "Chlorinated polyvinyl chloride") ,
(CPVC), as it is called, is produced by chlorination of aqueous solution of
suspension PVC particles followed by exposure to [ UV light
](/wiki/Ultraviolet "Ultraviolet") which initiates the free-radical
chlorination.  [9]

